  "notes": {
    "html": "Start here. HTML is the structure of every page — headings, links, forms, and content.\n",
    "html-basics": "Tags, attributes, and the document skeleton (`<!DOCTYPE html>`, `html`, `head`, `body`).\n",
    "semantic-html": "Use elements that describe meaning: `header`, `nav`, `main`, `article`, `section`, `footer`.\n",
    "seo-basics": "Titles, meta description, heading order, and alt text so pages can be found and understood.\n",
    "html-best-practices": "Valid markup, accessibility, and a clear outline before you add styling or scripts.\n",
    "css": "CSS paints the structure: layout, color, type, and how the page adapts to the screen.\n",
    "css-basics": "Selectors, the box model, cascade, and common properties for color, space, and type.\n",
    "responsive-design": "Flexible layouts, media queries, and mobile-first so the page works on any width.\n",
    "vcs": "Version control records history so you can branch, review, and undo with confidence.\n"
  },
